 >HEAD

   DATAID="MASKZ1"
   ACQBY="AusMT test fixture"
   PROSPECT="Impedance mask fixture"
   LOC="Fixture"
   LAT=-41.73
   LONG=147.72
   ELEV=  0.00

 >INFO   MAXLINES=1000

   MINTED FIXTURE - NOT CUSTODIAN DATA. The block layout and the fabricated
   impedance constants reproduce the shape of the 2002 FORTRAN conversion
   output held in the AusMT GDS staging at GDS/_staging/surveys - measured on
   tamar-tasmania-1980s/transfer_functions/edi/AVO.edi whose own banner reads
   "BOGUS IMPEDANCES ONLY FOR WINGLINK". No byte is copied from a staged file:
   the header identity is invented and the tipper values below are minted for
   this test. The point of the fixture is the impedance: ZXY and ZYX are the
   constant 1+1i that a survey declaring no electric channels cannot have
   measured.

 >=DEFINEMEAS

   MAXCHAN=7
   MAXRUN=999
   MAXMEAS=99999
   UNITS=M
   REFTYPE=CART
   REFLAT=-41.73:0:0
   REFLONG=147.72:0:0
   REFELEV=  0.00

 >HMEAS ID= 1001.001 CHTYPE=HX X = 0.  Y = 0.  AZM = 0.
 >HMEAS ID= 1002.001 CHTYPE=HY X = 0.  Y = 0.  AZM= 90.
 >HMEAS ID= 1003.001 CHTYPE=HZ X = 0.  Y = 0.  AZM= 0.
 >EMEAS ID= 1004.001 CHTYPE=EX X = -100.  Y = 0. X2 = 100.  Y2 = 0.
 >EMEAS ID= 1005.001 CHTYPE=EY X = 0.  Y = -100. X2 = 0.  Y2 = 100.

 >=MTSECT
